cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Control Evidence Object Model
message: >-
  If you use this specification, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A record model for what an AI agent is permitted to do, what it is expected
  to do, what it was observed doing, and the evidence for each. Twelve objects
  across four layers, with controlled vocabularies, a five-state evidence
  scale, seven reference states, a four-grade gap scale, a JSON schema and a
  reference validator. Addresses the gap left by agent identity and
  authorisation standards, which describe permissions but define no common
  schema for observed actions and the evidence for them.
